I was starting up a game with my daughter, who, quite naturally, wanted to
play the game with the 'female' option on.  Since this cannot be set while the
game is running, I edited the NETHACK.CNF file so that it was set.  I then
started up the game and hit the '!' key once character name and type had been
selected and the dungeon was drawn.  The game shelled out to DOS OK, but as
soon as I started up 'vi' (MKS Toolkit version) to edit the file, the system
crashed and I had to cold boot to get it started.

The version was 3.0 pl7, and I was running 4DOS 3.0 w/ MSDOS 3.3's system
files.  Needless to say, I have NOT repeated the procedure and simply try to
remember to edit the .cnf file just before I start up a new game instead.

